  "notes": [
    "DERIVED from the official schemas, never guessed: 19.2 IATA_AirShoppingRS.xsd against the 24.1 (formerly published as 21.3.6) distribution (IATA_AirShoppingRS.xsd plus its imported IATA_OffersAndOrdersCommonTypes.xsd). Names and paths from tools/compare-paths.py; every rule re-checked so the old name exists nowhere in 24.1 and the new one sits under the same parent.",
    "RESULT: every 19.2 reference response, translated, VALIDATES against the 24.1 XSD (tools/validate-translation.sh: round trip, one way, en/es/pt, three routes, offers recycled to 500).",
    "FLOW: the mock's own OfferPriceRS, OrderViewRS and OrderReshopRS, built in 19.2 shape and valid there, also VALIDATE against the 24.1 XSD through this mapping. Specific to them: OrderItem/Service/ServiceAssociations -> OrderServiceAssociation with PaxSegmentRefID wrapped in PaxSegmentRef; AddOfferItem -> AddedOfferItem; ReshopPrice/AddPrice -> PriceAndFareDetails. The reshop's Order key and the OrderView answer to a cancel (no OrderCancelRS after 19.2) are handled in code, because 19.2 has nothing to translate them from.",
    "SERVICES AND SEATS: the mock's ServiceListRS and SeatAvailabilityRS also VALIDATE against the 24.1 XSD. ALaCarteOffer/ALaCarteOfferItem -> OfferItem; Eligibility/FlightAssociations -> OfferFlightAssociations with PaxSegmentRefID wrapped in PaxSegmentReferences; each CabinCompartment/ColumnID in its own SeatColumn (wrapEach); seat-row-number repeats the row's RowNumber on every Seat, which 21.3 requires.",
    "REAL PROVIDER DATA (a live multi-city capture) needed three more rules: operated legs repeated under several segments are listed once in DatedOperatingLegList (dated-segments dedupes by ID); a service definition's own PaxSegmentRefID goes inside OfferFlightAssociations/PaxSegmentReferences (a nested wrap); and definition-owner gives each ServiceDefinition the OwnerCode 21.3 requires, taken from the document's offers.",
    "NAMESPACES: from 21.3 the root and its direct children are in http://www.iata.org/IATA/2015/EASD/00/IATA_OffersAndOrdersMessage; everything below is in ...IATA_OffersAndOrdersCommonTypes. The common types become the default namespace and the message-level names take the m: prefix.",
    "ORDER: every sequence in the 21.3+ common types is alphabetical, ignoring case (409 of 409 in 21.3, 426 of 426 in 24.1 and 24.4), so sortChildren reproduces the target order without per-type data.",
    "STRUCTURAL (code, edge/translate.go): dated-segments splits each PaxSegment into DatedMarketingSegment -> DatedOperatingSegment -> DatedOperatingLeg lists with derived one-to-one ids (DMS_/DOS_/LEG_ + PaxSegmentID); tz-into-datetime folds TimeZoneCode into the xs:dateTime value, lossless; weight-unit moves UnitCode to WeightUnitOfMeasurement in UN/ECE Rec 20 codes (KG->KGM, POUNDS->LBR); unpriced-penalties removes penalties with no amount, and their references, because Price became mandatory and inventing one would misstate the fare (the offer item's Change/CancelRestrictions still carry what they said).",
    "RENAMES: SeatProfile/CharacteristicCode -> SeatCharacteristicCode; Service/ServiceAssociations -> OfferServiceAssociation; BaggageFlightAssociations -> OfferFlightAssociations; scoped Offer/BaggageAllowance -> BaggageAssociations (DataLists' BaggageAllowance keeps its name). WRAPS: PaxSegmentRefID in PaxSegmentReferences, PaxJourneyRefID in PaxJourneyRef. HOIST: FareRule/PenaltyRefID up to FareDetail.",
    "DROPS (name absent from the target, or from that parent): Penalty/{AppCode,CancelFeeInd,ChangeFeeInd,UpgradeFeeInd,PenaltyPercent}; BaggageAllowance/ApplicableBagText; PieceAllowance/{ApplicablePartyText,Desc}; WeightAllowance/{ApplicablePartyText,DescText}; DataLists/{FareList,MediaList}; Offer/WebAddressURL (21.3 has it on OfferItem as WebAddressURI); ALaCarteOffer/OwnerTypeCode.",
    "VALUES: FarePriceTypeCode is a closed list from 21.3 (Filed, Net). The provider's SELL_AMOUNT is the selling price of a published fare, which is Filed.",
    "Scope: AirShoppingRS (one way, return, multi-city), OfferPriceRS, ServiceListRS, SeatAvailabilityRS, OrderViewRS and OrderReshopRS, for the elements the references and builders produce."
  ]
}
